  "kind": "build",
  "title": "# Orchestrator: cheap redundancy check at split time (Brett, Nov 7) Every time the orchestrator tak…",
  "asked": "# Orchestrator: cheap redundancy check at split time (Brett, Nov 7) Every time the orchestrator takes a build request and splits it into steps, it runs a CHEAP redundancy check before registering it. Plain code, zero AI tokens, fast (<2 s). 1. Check the new build and each of its steps against: builds store/orchestrator (all builds, any status), Plan Studio plans + blueprints, Shipped features/feature-ledger, open branches in /root/axf-builds (names + commit subjects), and the asset registry (ui-registry) for UI steps. 2. Matching: normalized title/summary similarity, shared keywords/ids, same files/assets touched, superseded rounds (-r2, -fable). Thresholds in orchestrator settings. 3. On a hit: don't block silently. Attach findings to the build (\"looks like X, Y\") with suggested action (reuse/extend existing, merge into, skip step, proceed). Default: proceed and flag; setting to hold for Brett. Phone alert (AmberX) when a likely duplicate is found, answerable in place. 4. Results feed the Maintenance redundancy-scan report (shared finding format; coordinate with build maintenance-redundancy-scan if it has landed, else define the shared format here). 5. Settings in place, from assets, no hard-coded styling. Tests with known duplicates from today's store (e.g. skins r2/r3/r4, shipped-features rounds, handoff-2 copies). Add to Shipped features. Progress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
